# NOTICE

superred-target-safeclawarena

This module is a port of SafeClawArena's container harness into a superred
Target. Original code in this module (the superred adaptation: the target
contract, the runtime driver, factories, and tests) is licensed MIT (see
LICENSE). It vendors SafeClawArena's container-side harness and reproduces its
execution/capture logic; the upstream MIT license text is preserved verbatim in
`src/safeclawarena_target/_vendor/safeclawarena/LICENSE` (and `LICENSES/SafeClawArena-MIT.txt`).

## Upstream: SafeClawArena

- Repository: https://github.com/sunblaze-ucb/SafeClawArena (commit a11f5cc)
- Paper: Niu et al., arXiv:2606.30755 (2026).
- License: MIT — Copyright (c) 2026 SafeClawBench Authors

### Vendored harness (verbatim, MIT), under `src/safeclawarena_target/_vendor/safeclawarena/`

- `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.nemoclaw`, `Dockerfile.seclaw` — platform images.
- `tools/sim-google/sim-google` — the simulated Google Workspace CLI.
- `tools/seclaw-agent-wrapper.js` — the SecLaw CLI transport wrapper.
- `scripts/reset_env.sh` — the per-task environment provisioner.
- `configs/` — platform + model + workspace baseline configs.

NOT vendored: `tools/ripgrep/rg` (a 6.3 MB prebuilt binary the Docker build does
not reference); install ripgrep via the image if a task needs it. The upstream
`scripts/judge.py` is not vendored — its judging half is ported into the
`safeclawarena-claim` package and its execution/capture half is ported into
`runtime.py`.

### Ported execution logic (MIT)

`src/safeclawarena_target/runtime.py` reproduces upstream `judge.py`'s platform
config, container lifecycle, session execution (HTTP gateway / SecLaw CLI), and
post-run state capture. End-to-end execution requires Docker and the platform
image. Deviations are documented in `ASSUMPTIONS.md`.

